// users.allowlist.json — EXAMPLE. Copy it to `users.allowlist.json` (repo
// root, next to target_deploy.sh) and edit THAT copy. The live file is
// GITIGNORED on purpose: it carries real passwords and is never committed or
// pushed. This .example IS committed and must never hold a real password.
//
// Format: ONE JSON object mapping email → password.
//   * usernames must be `*@hsbc.com` (auth_service.verify_username_format)
//   * passwords must be >= 6 characters (MIN_PASSWORD_LEN). A shorter entry is
//     dropped at container startup with a WARNING that names the account (never
//     the password) and its logins fail until the config is fixed (M1-D4)
//   * every deploy RE-SYNCS every entry (provision_user force=True): a new
//     email creates the account, an existing email resets its password and
//     revokes its live sessions. Workspaces/views are untouched.
//   * admin@hsbc.com is AUTO-MERGED with password 123456 when you omit it
//     (M1-D5: omitting it used to disable the admin account entirely)
//
// Comments: `//` FULL-LINE comments like these are stripped by
// target_deploy.sh before parsing. A trailing `// note` AFTER the JSON on the
// same line is NOT supported — it fails validation, the whole file is skipped
// (WARNING) and the container starts with the image default (admin only).
// Keep every comment on its own line.
{
    "admin@hsbc.com": "123456",
    "alice@hsbc.com": "change-me-alice",
    "bob@hsbc.com": "change-me-bob"
}
